---
source: crates/jailint/tests/rules.rs
---
warning[freestanding]: `Thread` needs an operating system: it builds only for WINDOWS, MACOS, LINUX and ANDROID
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:2:1
   |
 2 | #import "Thread";
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: use a module that works with `OS == .NONE`, or import it under `#if OS != .NONE`
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding

warning[freestanding]: `New` allocates with the default allocator
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:9:12
   |
 9 |     return New(int);
   |            ^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: the default allocator has no heap here: wrap the call in `push_allocator(...)`, or `push_context` with an allocator set
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding

warning[freestanding]: `array_add` allocates with the default allocator
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:14:5
   |
14 |     array_add(*items, 1);
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: the default allocator has no heap here: wrap the call in `push_allocator(...)`, or `push_context` with an allocator set
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding

warning[freestanding]: `tprint` allocates with the default allocator
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:19:12
   |
19 |     return tprint("n = %", n);
   |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: the default allocator has no heap here: wrap the call in `push_allocator(...)`, or `push_context` with an allocator set
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding

warning[freestanding]: `grow` reaches `New`, which allocates with the default allocator
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:23:12
   |
23 |     return grow();
   |            ^^^^^^
   |
   = help: the default allocator has no heap here: wrap the call in `push_allocator(...)`, or `push_context` with an allocator set
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding

warning[freestanding]: `factorial` calls itself, so its stack use has no bound
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:26:1
   |
26 | factorial :: (n: int) -> int {
   | ^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: rewrite it as a loop, or keep an explicit stack of a fixed size
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding

warning[freestanding]: `ping` is part of a call cycle (ping -> pong -> ping), so its stack use has no bound
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:31:1
   |
31 | ping :: (n: int) {
   | ^^^^
   |
   = help: rewrite it as a loop, or keep an explicit stack of a fixed size
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding

warning[freestanding]: `buffer_work` keeps 4 KiB of locals on the stack, past the limit of 1 KiB
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:39:1
   |
39 | buffer_work :: () {
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: keep the large locals in globals or a fixed pool, or raise `[lint.freestanding] max_frame_bytes`
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding

warning[freestanding]: `print` writes to the console, in an interrupt handler
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:45:5
   |
45 |     print("tick\n");
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: a handler must not print: set a flag or a counter and report it from the main loop
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding

warning[freestanding]: `lock` takes a lock, in an interrupt handler
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:50:5
   |
50 |     lock(*guard);
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: a handler must not take a lock: the code it interrupts may hold it. Use a flag or an atomic
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding

warning[freestanding]: `unlock` takes a lock, in an interrupt handler
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:51:5
   |
51 |     unlock(*guard);
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: a handler must not take a lock: the code it interrupts may hold it. Use a flag or an atomic
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding

warning[freestanding]: `sleep_milliseconds` may block, in an interrupt handler
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:52:5
   |
52 |     sleep_milliseconds(1);
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: a handler must return quickly: do not wait in it
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding

warning[freestanding]: `New` allocates with the default allocator, in an interrupt handler
  --> tests/lint/freestanding/bad.jai:53:13
   |
53 |     cell := New(int);
   |             ^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: a handler must not allocate: use storage set aside beforehand
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/freestanding
